## Request Routing

**Gate 1 — Complexity Gate** (the `thinking_os` rule): Q1 Cynefin (CLEAR/COMPLICATED/COMPLEX/CHAOTIC) → Q2 Dimension count. Record classification.

**Gate 2 — Request Type**: A (Question) → answer directly or Zoom. B (Task) → Core Loop. C (Ad-hoc) → trivial: inline{% if modules.tasks %}, else `cos task-create` first{% else %}, else treat as a Task{% endif %}. D (Audit) → verify command or Zoom first. Details: `docs/governance/agent-workflow.md`

## Core Loop

**Initialize → Classify → Orient → Plan → Execute → Verify & Close.** The cycle and its checklists are the `thinking_os` rule; this project's specifics:

- **Initialize** — `cos daily` (ONCE per session).{% if modules.tasks %} `cos task-start TASK-NNN`.{% endif %}
- **Classify** — record the gate: `bash .{{ agent_id }}/hooks/write-state.sh .thinking_os-gate "COMPLICATED 3"`; build the Read List from the SessionStart "Classify Read List" card. Domain routes: {{ substitutions.DOMAIN_ROUTES }}
{% if modules.memory %}- **Orient** — Memory Check: scan `.agents/memory/MEMORY.md`; open the memory file of any line that touches the task.
{% endif %}- **Plan** — invoke the domain skill: {{ substitutions.SKILL_ROUTES }}. For COMPLICATED+, write Problem Framing to Notes and record `bash .{{ agent_id }}/hooks/write-state.sh .zoom-checkpoint "PROBLEM_FRAMED"`.
- **Verify & Close** — run the Verification Matrix commands below.{% if modules.tasks %} Fail 2x → `cos task-block TASK-NNN --reason "..."`; pass → `cos task-move TASK-NNN --to testing`, then `cos task-done TASK-NNN`.{% else %} Fail 2x → stop and surface to the user.{% endif %}{% if modules.memory %} A lesson a future session needs → a memory file in `.agents/memory/` plus its index line.{% endif %}
